                <pb facs="0240" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 21641/15.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Carter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 29.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The department has received your No. 63 of
                    the 9th instant, in regard to the extradition of Vahan Nalbandian, and commends
                    the legation upon its manner of procedure in this case.</p>
                <p>You will convey to the appropriate Servian and Austrian officials the thanks of
                    the department for the courtesy extended in the matter of transit.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
